---
description: Playwright E2E patterns for Next.js and Fastify API
glob: "apps/next/e2e/**/*, apps/next/playwright.config.ts, apps/fastify/test/**/*, apps/fastify/playwright.config.ts"
---

## Config
- No webServer; URLs from `PLAYWRIGHT_APP_URL` / `PLAYWRIGHT_API_URL` (env or `--app` / `--api` params)
- Fastify: only `--api` param; `test:e2e` = URL-based, `test:e2e:local` = spawn API, poll, run, cleanup
- Param format: `--app=URL` or `--app URL`, `--api=URL` or `--api URL`
- CI: test:e2e:local only (spawn local servers; no Vercel URLs)
- Local: Next `test:e2e:local` = spawn Fastify + Next, poll, run, kill. Fastify `test:e2e:local` = spawn API only. Root `pnpm test:e2e` = run both via scripts/run-e2e.mjs
- workers: 1, fullyParallel: false — PGLite does not support concurrent writers; tests must run in series
- projects: auth first (magic-link, wallet-auth, link-wallet, wallet-metamask-auth, wallet-solana-auth), then chromium (chat-assistant); link-email disabled

## Session Model
- Context = browser profile; authenticatedPage = single shared page reused across all authed tests (worker-scoped)
- One login per worker, then navigate and assert. No per-test login for authed tests
- Session reused via worker-scoped storageState (saved after login, new context per test)
- **Disabled specs**: link-email excluded via testIgnore

## Test Order
- Auth project first: magic-link-auth, wallet-auth, link-wallet, wallet-metamask-auth, wallet-solana-auth (wallet specs use auth-helpers or fixtures-wallet-mock/fixtures-solana-mock)
- Chromium project: chat-assistant (uses authenticatedPage; fixture triggers magic link login)

## Disabled Specs
- link-email excluded via testIgnore; chat-assistant skipped (test.describe.skip) until getAuthToken fixed for chat transport

## Auth Fixtures
- Login/logout tests: import `@playwright/test`, use `page` (fresh context per test)
- Authed feature tests: import from `e2e/fixtures`, use `authenticatedPage`; no `loginAsTestUser` in test body
- Wallet specs: wallet-auth, link-wallet use auth-helpers; wallet-metamask-auth, wallet-solana-auth use mock fixtures
- Each authed test must navigate to its target route (e.g. `authenticatedPage.goto('/')`) since the same page is reused

## Test Email
- Use `test@test.ai` when `ALLOW_TEST` enabled; token from DB (`/test/magic-link/last`), no fake outbox. Unit tests with `setTestEmailProvider` can use any email; only E2E magic-link flow requires `@test.ai`.
